Z||000000||loren||03-17-2001||09:37 PM||||i (think) that i would like to eleminate the cat on an 85gt 6 cyl.and replace it with an adapter..does anyone know where i might purchase one ?<P>Loren||||reg||1
Z||000001||Mark||03-17-2001||09:48 PM||||Rodney sells one in stainless steel.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com/retail.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.rodneydickman.com/retail.html</A> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||skitime||03-17-2001||10:43 PM||||It is just a 2 1/8 inch pipe 21 inches long. I have one for $5 plus shipping but just go to a parts store.||||reg||1
Z||000003||skitime||03-17-2001||10:50 PM||||BTW the reson I have it is I removed it and replaced it with a cherry bomb muffler.  It is a straight through muffler with no restrictions.  You can look straight through it.  It is quieter than a cat yet has no restrictions.  You can get it at Pep Boys for $14 and change about the same as a straight pipe. The muffler is 23 inches long and 2 1/4 openings so you need to cut about 1/2 inch off each end and use a 3/4 long 2 1/8 adapter inside the ends. If you want loud use the straight pipe it does sound cool.||||reg||1
Z||000004||danny boy||03-18-2001||02:13 AM||||Just make sure when you cut off the cat. you cut the welds and pull the pipe out. If you cut the pipe there won't be enough room to attatch the replacement pipe.||||reg||1
